{{~##
   One table per page: the header rows describing its columns, then its data.

   It used to be every table on one page. A workbook whose largest table has 100,000
   rows made that page 37 MB, so the other 66 tables in it could not be read at all -
   and the size is the data's, not something to tune away. One page per table means the
   page a reader opens is the size of the table they asked for.

   The header shows the sheet's own columns rather than the folded groups, so the page
   reads like the workbook it documents. A column that folded into a group names that
   group in a tooltip.

   What refers to this table comes with it. The type column has always linked outward -
   this column points at that table - and the question a reader actually arrives with is
   the other direction: what points here.
##~}}
{{~ include 'html-head.sbn' ~}}
<p class="lead"><svg class="i"><use href="#i-table"></use></svg>{{ source_link }} &middot; 행 {{ record_count }}개 &middot; 컬럼 {{ column_count }}개{{ if sheet_column_count != '' }} <span class="hint">(시트 컬럼 {{ sheet_column_count }}개)</span>{{ end }}{{ if source_cell != '' }} <span class="hint">&middot; {{ source_cell }}</span>{{ end }}</p>
{{~ if comment != '' ~}}
<p class="comment">{{ comment }}</p>
{{~ end ~}}
{{~ if referenced_by | array.size > 0 ~}}
<p class="hint">이 테이블을 가리키는 컬럼:
{{~ for item in referenced_by ~}}
<a href="{{ item.href }}">{{ item.name }}</a>{{ if !for.last }}, {{ end }}
{{~ end ~}}
</p>
{{~ end ~}}
<div data-table>
<div class="tools">
<input type="search" data-filter="rows" placeholder="행 필터">
<span class="hint" data-shown>{{ shown_count }}행 중 {{ shown_count }}행</span>
{{~ if truncated ~}}
<span class="warn">{{ record_count }}행 중 처음 {{ shown_count }}행입니다. 더 보려면 recipe의 MaxRowsPerTable을 올리세요.</span>
{{~ end ~}}
{{~## The three marks a cell may hold, said once for the table rather than only in a tooltip.
     A polymorphic group's columns are the union of every variant's, so most cells of such a
     table hold the「이 변종에 없음」mark - and a dash beside an italic `null` differs by too
     little for a reader who has not been told which is which. ##~}}
{{~ if has_variants ~}}
<span class="hint"><span class="na">&mdash;</span> 그 행의 변종에 없는 멤버 &middot; <span class="null">null</span> 값이 없음</span>
{{~ end ~}}
</div>
<div class="scroll">
<table id="table_{{ name }}"{{ if sortable }} data-sortable{{ end }}>
<thead>
<tr class="names">
{{~ for cell in name_cells ~}}
{{ cell }}
{{~ end ~}}
</tr>
{{~ if has_column_comments ~}}
<tr class="about">
{{~ for cell in comment_cells ~}}
{{ cell }}
{{~ end ~}}
</tr>
{{~ end ~}}
<tr class="types">
{{~ for cell in type_cells ~}}
{{ cell }}
{{~ end ~}}
</tr>
<tr class="side">
{{~ for cell in side_cells ~}}
{{ cell }}
{{~ end ~}}
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
{{~ for row in rows ~}}
<tr>{{ row.cells | array.join '' }}</tr>
{{~ end ~}}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
{{~ if row_previews != '' ~}}
{{~## The rows this page's references name, for the panel that shows one without following
     the link. In a hidden element rather than a script tag: a sheet value may read like a
     url, and the check that no page fetches anything looks at script tags. ##~}}
<div id="rowdefs" hidden>{{ row_previews }}</div>
{{~ end ~}}
{{ include 'html-foot.sbn' }}
